    "evidence_text": " The Chancellery's seat from 1875 was the former city palace of Prince Antoni Radziwi\u0142\u0142 (1775\u20131833) on Wilhelmstra\u00dfe in Berlin.\n\n Its seat is at the former city palace of Prince Eugene of Savoy in the Austrian capital Vienna.\n\nWinter Palace of Prince Eugene\n\nThe Winter Palace of Prince Eugene (German: \"Winterpalais Prinz Eugen\" ), also known as the City Palace (German: \"Stadtpalais\" ), is a high-Baroque palace in the Innere Stadt district of Vienna, Austria.\n\n Located on a narrow street at Himmelpfortgasse 8, the palace was used as the winter residence of Prince Eugene of Savoy, who spent his summers at the Belvedere.\n\n The Winter Palace was designed and constructed by Johann Bernhard Fischer von Erlach from 1695 to 1700, and by Johann Lukas von Hildebrandt from 1702 to 1724 following his predecessor's plans.\n\nErna Flegel\n\nErna Flegel (11 July 1911 \u2013 16 February 2006) was a German nurse.",
